    "numeric_note": ">80%, 3 mm",
    "theory_text": "Quick Notes\n•Most common intraocular malignancies: Secondaries (metastases)\n•Primary intraocular malignancies: uncommon\n • Children: Retinoblastoma\n • Adults: Choroidal melanoma\nUveal Malignancies\n•Most common primary uveal malignancy (>80%): Choroidal melanoma\n•Risk factors: More common in fair-skinned individuals\n•Location: Usually within 3 mm of optic disc\n•Metastasis: Most commonly to the liver"
