    "numeric_note": "7th–8th decades, 1156",
    "theory_text": "Quick Notes\nSebaceous Carcinoma\n•Occurs mostly in elderly (7th–8th decades)\n•Common site: Upper lid\n•Arises from sebaceous glands & glands of Zeis at lash roots\n•Red flags:\n  • Older patient with recurrent chalazion\n  • Chronic unilateral blepharitis or conjunctivitis\n•Management: Biopsy to confirm diagnosis"
  },
